questions.explanation:
Count the different types of hydrogen atoms:
(a) the nine H of the three equivalent $CH_3$ groups on C-2 give $ClCH_2C(CH_3)_2CH_2CH_3$;
(b) the $CH_2$ hydrogens give $(CH_3)_3CCHClCH_3$;
(c) the terminal $CH_3$ hydrogens give $(CH_3)_3CCH_2CH_2Cl$.
C-2 is quaternary and carries no H, so three structural isomers form.
Answer: (2)
